[38;5;231m⏺[39m I've opened a sketch of three layouts in a browser tab. If it didn't open, here's the link:
  [94m]8;id=197xzwv;http://localhost:64569/?key=9e8a045b311096c598281df7c8a76ca8ba5be5292789bea96c123b52ec20c1e3\http://localhost:64569/?key=9e8a045b311096c598281df7c8a76ca8ba5be5292789bea96c123b52ec20c1e3[39m]8;;\

  The sketches are token-heavy, so tell me if you'd rather stay in the terminal. They're saved under [38;5;153m.hyperpowers/[39m, and
  the repo has no [38;5;153m.gitignore[39m, so you'll want to add that folder to one.

  All three options include a "Showing X of 48 events" line that screen readers announce when results change.

  - [1mA: filter bar above the table.[0m The controls are always visible: event type, a device or location search, and a
    "Failed sign-ins only" checkbox. It's the easiest to find and the simplest to build, but it adds a row of height.
  - [1mB: a "Filter" button that opens a popover[0m, with active filters shown as removable tags. The page stays clean, and
    the guidelines already name a filter panel as a use for popovers. But the filters sit behind a click, and the people
    who most need them would have to know to click it.
  - [1mC: preset chips plus search[0m (All, Failed sign-ins, Sign-ins, Account changes, API tokens). Failed sign-ins are one
    click away. But the guidelines have no chip component, so we'd have to propose a new variant in
    [38;5;153mdocs/ui-guidelines/02[39m first. That means an extra review step.

  I recommend A. Your notes say people come to this page to find a failed sign-in they don't recognize, so the filters
  should be visible without a click. A also uses only components that already exist in 02 and 03.

  Which layout do you want? You can click one in the browser too. After that I'll ask which filters to include.

